<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40026" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quartārĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A fourth part</i>, <i>quarter</i> of
			any measure, esp. of a sextarius, <i>a quartern</i>,
				<i>gill</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sumito bituminis tertiarium, et sulphuris
					quartarium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 95, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					47</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mellis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 5, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">farris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 3, 3, § 9</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mule-driver</i>, <i>muleteer</i>,
			who received a fourth part of the profits, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				258</span></i> Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
